<title>AUSTRIA: Bank Austria to buy out small CA shareholders.</title>
<headline>Bank Austria to buy out small CA shareholders.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Vice Chancellor Wolfgang Schuessel said on Sunday Bank Austria had offered to buy out small shareholders of Creditanstalt.</p>
<p>He also told reporters that the state's 19 percent stake in Bank Austria would be sold via the stock exchange.  </p>
<p>Schuessel, speaking to reporters after marathon coalition crisis talks over the CA privatisation, said Creditanstalt would remain independent for at least five years after its sale to Bank Austria.</p>
</text>
